[{"code":"top_level_list_changed","severity":"error","span":{"file":"tests/corpus/check/bad/inline/RecursiveClassGrowth.beni","start":{"line":24,"col":9},"end":{"line":24,"col":30}},"title":"TOP-LEVEL LIST CHANGED","message":"`List.push` changes `(a 1) ⊤` in place, but it is `shared`, a top-level value.\n\n24|bad ⊤ = List.push ((a 1) ⊤) 2\n           ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ the list is changed in place here\n\n3|shared = [ 1 ]\n  ^^^^^^ the top-level list is defined here\n\nA top-level value is shared by every part of the program and never changes:\nchanged in place, it would change for every part that reads it.\n\nMake `shared` a function that builds a fresh value at each call, or change a\ncopy: `List.copy shared`.\n\nThis is the language's rule for top-level values, whether or not anything else\nreads the list (ownership-checker.md §4.2)."}]
